  "title": "Union Eyes V2 staging: preserving startup and full base persona verification",
  "description": "Continue qualified Union Eyes V2 base-release repairs and full persona verification on the dedicated staging stack under the standing solo-founder authorization. Current application source 6a60c95c9de17e9343e0414bb51766afbc190054 and immutable build 45214964440 are qualified; the final bound operator must pass its own checks and normal admission before protected zero-traffic preparation, rollback rehearsal, exact-plan preserving upgrade and readiness/version-gated cutover. Preserve all live rows, sequences, original roles/ACLs, migration/bootstrap history and human accounts. Seven navigation profiles are only a subset of the 26 required stakeholder families and 34 required role boundaries. Historical candidate bindings and failed runs remain in the linked evidence. Finance implementation, production, Phase 3B and live-data resets remain excluded.",
  "service": "union-eyes",
  "environment": "STAGING",
  "change_type": "NORMAL",
  "risk_level": "HIGH",
  "impact_summary": "Update only the qualified dedicated Union Eyes V2 staging workload. Preserve existing live staging data, all 40 installed immutable migrations and the known overlay; no primary schema replay or empty-target restore. No production resource, client data, production DNS, financial settlement or institutional authority is in scope.",
