  "rollback_plan": "For the data-preserving forward upgrade, a failure before commit rolls back the entire transaction and verifies the original catalog; all original rows, sequences and migration/bootstrap history must remain unchanged. After commit, CCC cannot admit the upgraded schema: preserve the upgraded database and recover forward to the qualified 6a60c95c9de17e9343e0414bb51766afbc190054 image through readiness/version-gated staging cutover or the existing protected staging rollout. Do not route to a schema-incompatible old image, reverse schema, reset data or touch production. For other staging changes, a prior digest/revision can be restored only after its schema compatibility is proven. Retain all failure and recovery evidence.",
